# 7 Days in Hell — working rules

- This is a Decentraland SDK7 scene (`@dcl/sdk` 7.29). Reference material lives in `dclcontext/` — read `sdk7-complete-reference.md` before guessing an API.
- Mobile first. Every interaction must work with a single tap: no hover, no keyboard-only paths, no drag. Buttons are >= 64 virtual px tall. UI is laid out on a 1600x720 virtual canvas (`src/ui/theme.ts`).
- Balance numbers live only in `src/config/balance.ts`; world positions only in `src/config/geometry.ts`. Never hard-code them in systems.
- Visual assets resolve through `src/art/catalog.ts`. Do not reference model paths anywhere else.
- Gameplay entities are pooled (`systems/*`). Do not `engine.addEntity()` inside a per-frame system.
- Game flow changes go through `src/core/game.ts`; systems only read `state.phase`.
- Reused original content (video URLs, dialogue text, audio files) must stay verbatim: `src/config/dialogue.ts`, `src/config/media.ts`, `sounds/`.
- Verify with `npm run build` (bundle + typecheck) before committing.
